# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored - never commit real keys.
#   cp .env.example .env
# Then: npm start

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One key for everything: translation, prescription parsing, speech recognition.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Get one at https://console.groq.com/keys
#
# Groq replaced Gemini here because Gemini's free tier is a ~20 requests PER DAY
# budget - one consultation spends about six, so a free Gemini key supported
# roughly three consultations a day and then failed until midnight. Groq's free
# tier is a standing per-minute quota instead, with no card and no expiry:
#   language model   1,000 requests/day, 30 requests/minute
#   speech-to-text   2,000 requests/day, 20 requests/minute, 28,800 audio s/day
# That is about 8 hours of transcription every day, free.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides.
# PORT=3000

# Language model. openai/gpt-oss-120b is the default: the strongest of the free
# models at translation into Indian languages and the most reliable at returning
# strict JSON. Cheaper/smaller fallbacks, same key, no other change needed:
#   qwen/qwen3.8-27b        lighter, very good at Indian scripts
#   openai/gpt-oss-20b      fastest, noticeably weaker on translation
# GROQ_CHAT_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# whisper-large-v3 is more accurate but slower and 3x the price.
# GROQ_STT_MODEL=whisper-large-v3-turbo

# Set to 1 if you are on a paid Groq plan, which raises the upload cap from
# 25 MB to 100 MB.
# GROQ_PAID=0